## Day files with fidelity n/a that were NOT changed (24), by category

D = derivation or definition from the author's own assumptions; C = cites a source whose own row is accurate or verified; Q = qualitative or position statement. Claim-level reading, not a full re-read. Human Ne about 1e4 is a contested-standard input (rule F): exempt from citation, flagged, and any node whose conclusion depends on it carries `external: contested`.

- A: D (formula node; inputs are scored in A1-A3)
- A4: D (definition; the estimate is A4a)
- A4d: D (describes the paper's choice)
- B1: C (cites Kimura-Ohta, accurate; Chalub is B1e)
- B1a: C (Kimura-Ohta first moment, accurate)
- B1b: D (derived from 4Ne)
- B2d: Q (qualitative)
- B3f: D (own inputs, standard values)
- B3h: C (Keightley cited, partial in the table)
- C1a: Q
- C5a: C (Keightley cited, verified)
- D2i: C (Schutzenberger quote, accurate)
- D9: D (hypothetical parameters, 'Under N = ...')
- F2: Q (proposed check)
- F4a: Q
- G1: C (Good verified)
- G4: Q
- G4b: D
- Gb: D (own model)
- Ge: Q
- H10: C (Keightley cited, H7)
- ROOT: Q
